<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.3.4: Writing an Equation to Represent a Relationship</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00087</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.3.4: Writing an Equation to Represent a Relationship</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b0ce9138-7bf7-4075-9984-f87e3b731ce4</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<para>Clare volunteers at a local library during the summer. Her work includes putting labels on 750 books.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>How many minutes will she need to finish labeling all books if she takes no breaks and labels <emphasis>10 books a minute?
  </emphasis></item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 75 minutes</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>How many minutes will she need to finish labeling all books if she takes no breaks and labels <emphasis>15 books a minute?</emphasis> </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 50 minutes</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Suppose Clare labels the books at a constant speed of \(s\) books per minute. Write an equation that represents
    the relationship between her labeling speed and the number of minutes it would take her to finish labeling.</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \( s * m=750 \) or \( m= \frac{750}{s} \), where \(m\) is the number of minutes and \(s\) is
  the speed in books per minute.</para>
<title>Response to Student Thinking</title>
<title>More Chances</title>
<para>Students will have more opportunities to understand the mathematical ideas in this cool-down, so there is no need to
  slow down or add additional work to the next lessons. Instead, use the results of this cool-down to provide guidance
  for what to look for and emphasize over the next several lessons to support students in advancing their current
  understanding.</para></section>
</content>
